# grid 3x3, seed 0, pack mode: row
# rows 20, alternatives 72, rows with choices 17
# period (frame) 14 cycles, max injection clock 11
# worst-case wait from period start to any destination: <= 11 clocks
# per-destination repeat rate: once every 14 cycles
# aggregate throughput: 20/14 = 1.43 packets per cycle
# tight latency: one packet per row per period (20 of 72 pairs fire); destinations sharing a row are mutually exclusive; rotating choices cover all pairs in 4 periods
# command: python3 -m routing generate-bf --grid 3 --seed 0 --pack row
